  "notes": [
    "Markers are removed before the engine sees source; positions use UTF-16 code units.",
    "Find references excludes declarations. Expected sets must match exactly, not merely contain expected locations.",
    "Two reference tests explicitly accept either the final identifier range or the full qualified-expression range observed from FCS; occurrence-set equality remains exact.",
    "FCS may return either .fsi or .fs for an exported definition; both are explicitly accepted for this exploratory fixture.",
    "The API edit deliberately makes consumers ill-typed; stale exact results are unacceptable. Baseline behavior must be compared before claiming feature parity.",
    "Linked-file cases require per-project defines. A path-only source index cannot truthfully mark both answers exact.",
    "The first29 queries are preserved unchanged in expectations.original29.json. New property/record cases are independent F# programs checked by the real FCS oracle.",
    "Per-occurrence qualifiedFrom alternatives permit explicitly marked full-receiver ranges as well as the member token, without accepting extra, missing or arbitrary spans."
  ]
}
